  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Malaria - Sierra Leone (01-Jul-2016-30-Jun-2018)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sierra Leone, Malaria, Catholic Relief Services - United States Conference of Catholic Bishops (CRS Sierra Leone)This program has the following goals: By 2020, reduce malaria morbidity and mortality by at least 40% compared with 2015.. The objectives of this program are: All malaria cases to receive effective treatment..  All suspected malaria cases should have access to confirmatory diagnosis.  By 2020, at least 95% of health facilities report routinely on malaria programme performance..  By 2020, maintain and strengthen capacity for program management, coordination and partnership to achieve malaria programme performance at all levels..  Provide access to 100% of the population at risk with preventive measures by 2017.  To protect at least 80 % of pregnant women and children under one year with IPT 3 by 2020.  To provide knowledge to the population such that at least 80% practise malaria prevention and treatment measures by 2018.</narrative>
  </description>
